<title>UK: Yorkshire says Stuart Wallis to be chairman.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire says Stuart Wallis to be chairman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yorkshire Group Plc, formerly known as Yorkshire Chemicals, said on Monday that it had appointed Stuart Wallis as its next chairman.</p>
<p>He will take over from Phillip Lowe from October 1 1996. Lowe has headed up the group since 1987 and is due to retire from the board.</p>
<p>The company statement said Wallis had experience in the U.S., European and Asian markets and a proven track record in development of business strategies.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
